reusing `--session-id` on an existing session; the spec uses `--resume`.\n- **cursor:** `--resume <session_id from the result line>` (`cursor/resume-answer`) answers `392`.\n\n### Errors\n\n- **cursor** (`cursor/error-bad-model`): exits 1 with empty stdout. stderr holds the message and the list of valid models.\n- **pi** (`pi/error-bad-model`): **exits 0**. stderr warns `Model \"no-such-model\" not found … Using custom model id.` The stream ends normally with `agent_end`, whose last message has `stopReason: \"error\"` and `errorMessage: \"Codex error: The 'no-such-model' model is not supported …\"`. The parser must read `stopReason`, not the exit code.\n- **claude** (`claude/error-bad-model`): exits 1. stdout has a `result` line with `subtype: \"success\"`, `is_error: true` and the message in `result`. stderr has `[claude-code:unrecognized_model]`. The parser must read `is_error`, not `subtype`.\n\n### Cancelled (SIGTERM to the CLI)\n\nAll three backends exit 143 and stop mid-stream (`*/cancelled`). No `result` or `agent_end` line is written. The supervisor marks CANCELLED itself; nothing in the stream says so.\n\n### NEEDS_CONTEXT\n\nAll three backends end with a question and `STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT` in the final text (`*/needs-context`). In a first attempt, cursor searched widely before asking (its own transcript store, `env`, a filesystem glob), which produced a 960KB stream that held the user's MCP tool descriptors. The committed fixture was re-recorded with \"do not search, ask me\".\n\n### Redaction\n\nRaw streams carry the recording user's setup: pi's system-prompt `sections` and extension `toolsAdded`, and Claude's `system/init` lists and `hook_response` output. `scripts/redact.jq` blanks these and keeps the event shapes. `record.sh` applies it and replaces the home-directory name. Any live test that records fixtures (#17 and the per-backend live tests) must use the same filter.\n\n### Cost and usage\n\n- **claude:** `total_cost_usd` on the result line.\n- **cursor:** the result line has `usage` with `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, `cacheReadTokens` and `cacheWriteTokens`, and no cost.\n- **pi:** `usage.cost` appears on messages. The `agent_end` last-message cost (`$0.00016` in `pi/tool-calls-fix`) looks per-message. #16 should verify whether the run total needs summing over `message_end` events.\n\n### Stream noise the parsers must skip\n\n- **claude:** `system/hook_started`, `system/hook_response` (4 of them from user hooks), `system/commands_changed` and `rate_limit_event` arrive before the assistant turn.\n- **pi:** `entry_appended` and `turn_*`, and a final `agent_settled` after `agent_end`.\n- **cursor:** `thinking/delta` and `thinking/completed`.\n\n\n--\n","localExecutionTimeMs":1380},"isBackground":false},"description":"View issue #4 spec and comments"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_fca866d8-f4d2-4eae-9395-d1e67484877","startedAtMs":"1790845451737","completedAtMs":"1790845453929"},"model_call_id":"e585ae89-c308-48e6-a816-313689ff8cab-0-gxxy","session_id":"7bb334b3-f226-467c-b3bf-a467f772d57f","timestamp_ms":1790845453892}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"tool_e62da98b-fa48-4989-b8d9-9fb28291000","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures && for n in 7 9 10 11; do echo \"=== ISSUE $n ===\"; gh issue view $n --comments; done","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"tool_e62da98b-fa48-4989-b8d9-9fb28291000","simpleCommands":["cd","echo","gh"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":false,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"cd","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures"}],"fullText":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures"},{"name":"echo","args":[{"type":"string","value":"\"=== ISSUE $n ===\""}],"fullText":"echo \"=== ISSUE $n ===\""},{"name":"gh","args":[{"type":"word","value":"issue"},{"type":"word","value":"view"},{"type":"simple_expansion","value":"$n"},{"type":"word","value":"--comments"}],"fullText":"gh issue view $n --comments"}],"hasRedirects":false,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"redirects":[]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"View issues 7,9,10,11 with comments","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"7bb334b3-f226-467c-b3bf-a467f772d57f","adminCommandDenylist":[],"requestId":"e585ae89-c308-48e6-a816-313689ff8cab"},"result":{"success":{"command":"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-fixtures && for n in 7 9 10 11; do echo \"=== ISSUE $n ===\"; gh issue view $n --comments; done","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"=== ISSUE 7 ===\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings (owner, 2026-10-01)\n\n1. Real detached supervisor; the status file is the only source of truth. The MCP `job_registry` stays untouched until #13.\n2. Record path: `$TMPDIR/delegate-jobs/<uuid>.json`.\n3. Record shape: whatever is cheapest to implement and parse. That means the existing `PollResult` JSON (camelCase) plus `supervisorPid`, `heartbeatAt` and `resume {model, cwd, capability, sessionId}`.\n4. Heartbeat: 30s by default. Tests shorten it with a `DELEGATE_HEARTBEAT_MS` environment override. The supervisor is a separate process, so a fake clock cannot be shared with it.\n5. `watch`: one JSON line per job, in argument order. Exit 0 when all are terminal. On timeout, print the current records and exit 1.\n6. `watch` on an unknown job id exits 2 at once.\n7. Bad input to `run` (unknown model, empty prompt) exits 2 with the reason on stderr. An unknown model also lists the valid ids.\n8. The CLI appends only the STATUS-line instruction. The MCP prompt path is unchanged.\n9. A status-record write failure makes the supervisor exit non-zero. A supervisor that dies leaving RUNNING is deferred to #9.\n10. A second `[[bin]]` named `delegate` in `src/bin/delegate.rs`, sharing the library.\n\n--\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\nClarification on ruling 3: the heartbeat field is `lastHeartbeatAt`, reused from `PollResult`, not a new `heartbeatAt`.\n--\n=== ISSUE 9 ===\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings (owner, 2026-10-01)\n\n1. **BUSY:** a second read-write `run` or `resume` in a locked cwd prints `BUSY <holderJobId>` on stderr and exits 3.\n2. **Gate timeout:** the gate is killed if it runs past the job's tool-idle window (`--tool-idle-ms`, default 1800s). There is no new flag.\n3. **Lock:** `flock` on `$TMPDIR/delegate-locks/<hash of canonical cwd>.lock`, held by the supervisor. The file holds the job id.\n4. **Idle defaults:** model-idle 300s and tool-idle 1800s, carried over from the host profile.\n5. **Change-set:** always lists the commits made during the run, plus a concern if the tree is still dirty. The #6 probe showed a delegated Claude commits on its own branch.\n6. **MCP:** the old MCP `cursor_run` path does not take the file lock. That gap is accepted until #13 deletes MCP.\n7. **Dead supervisor** (deferred from #7): stale-heartbeat handling belongs here.\n--\n=== ISSUE 10 ===\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings (owner, 2026-10-01)\n\n1. **Output:** `resume` prints the new job id, like `run`.\n2. **Cancel on a terminal job:** a no-op. It prints the record and exits 0.\n3. **Resume errors:** `resume` on a RUNNING job, or on a record with no session id, exits 2 with the reason on stderr.\n4. **Chain links:** resuming A as B writes `supersededBy: B` into A's record and `resumedFrom: A` into B's. This keeps the reason MCP added the pointer (commit 8b21892): a watcher on a resumed NEEDS_CONTEXT record must be able to follow the chain instead of acting on the stale question.\n5. **Cancel:** SIGTERM to the supervisor's process group, then SIGKILL after 5s. If `cancel` had to SIGKILL, it writes CANCELLED itself.\n6. **Busy cwd:** a read-write resume into a locked cwd follows the #9 BUSY ruling (stderr `BUSY <holder>`, exit 3).\n--\n=== ISSUE 11 ===\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings (owner, 2026-10-01)\n\n1. **`delegate models`:** an aligned text table with id, label, backend and $in/$out per 1M tokens. The default is marked `*`. Rows sort by backend, then id.\n2. **`delegate doctor`:** human-readable text on stdout, one ok/warn/fail line per check. Missing or renamed models are warnings. It exits 0 when there are only warnings, and 1 on a hard failure (binary missing, or not logged in).\n3. **pi and claude models before #16/#17 land:** `run` exits 2 with `backend not implemented`, and `doctor` prints a skip line for each.\n4. **Model table:** `backend` replaces `family`. The ids are the 13 listed in #11 and spec story 45. Grok 4.7 is priced as Grok 4.6.\n--\n","stderr":"","executionTime":5119,"interleavedOutput":"=== ISSUE 7 ===\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings (owner, 2026-10-01)\n\n1. Real detached supervisor; the status file is the only source of truth. The MCP `job_registry` stays untouched until #13.\n2. Record path: `$TMPDIR/delegate-jobs/<uuid>.json`.\n3. Record shape: whatever is cheapest to implement and parse. That means the existing `PollResult` JSON (camelCase) plus `supervisorPid`, `heartbeatAt` and `resume {model, cwd, capability, sessionId}`.\n4. Heartbeat: 30s by default. Tests shorten it with a `DELEGATE_HEARTBEAT_MS` environment override. The supervisor is a separate process, so a fake clock cannot be shared with it.\n5. `watch`: one JSON line per job, in argument order. Exit 0 when all are terminal. On timeout, print the current records and exit 1.\n6. `watch` on an unknown job id exits 2 at once.\n7. Bad input to `run` (unknown model, empty prompt) exits 2 with the reason on stderr. An unknown model also lists the valid ids.\n8. The CLI appends only the STATUS-line instruction. The MCP prompt path is unchanged.\n9. A status-record write failure makes the supervisor exit non-zero. A supervisor that dies leaving RUNNING is deferred to #9.\n10. A second `[[bin]]` named `delegate` in `src/bin/delegate.rs`, sharing the library.\n\n--\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\nClarification on ruling 3: the heartbeat field is `lastHeartbeatAt`, reused from `PollResult`, not a new `heartbeatAt`.\n--\n=== ISSUE 9 ===\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings (owner, 2026-10-01)\n\n1. **BUSY:** a second read-write `run` or `resume` in a locked cwd prints `BUSY <holderJobId>` on stderr and exits 3.\n2. **Gate timeout:** the gate is killed if it runs past the job's tool-idle window (`--tool-idle-ms`, default 1800s). There is no new flag.\n3. **Lock:** `flock` on `$TMPDIR/delegate-locks/<hash of canonical cwd>.lock`, held by the supervisor. The file holds the job id.\n4. **Idle defaults:** model-idle 300s and tool-idle 1800s, carried over from the host profile.\n5. **Change-set:** always lists the commits made during the run, plus a concern if the tree is still dirty. The #6 probe showed a delegated Claude commits on its own branch.\n6. **MCP:** the old MCP `cursor_run` path does not take the file lock. That gap is accepted until #13 deletes MCP.\n7. **Dead supervisor** (deferred from #7): stale-heartbeat handling belongs here.\n--\n=== ISSUE 10 ===\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings (owner, 2026-10-01)\n\n1. **Output:** `resume` prints the new job id, like `run`.\n2. **Cancel on a terminal job:** a no-op. It prints the record and exits 0.\n3. **Resume errors:** `resume` on a RUNNING job, or on a record with no session id, exits 2 with the reason on stderr.\n4. **Chain links:** resuming A as B writes `supersededBy: B` into A's record and `resumedFrom: A` into B's. This keeps the reason MCP added the pointer (commit 8b21892): a watcher on a resumed NEEDS_CONTEXT record must be able to follow the chain instead of acting on the stale question.\n5. **Cancel:** SIGTERM to the supervisor's process group, then SIGKILL after 5s. If `cancel` had to SIGKILL, it writes CANCELLED itself.\n6. **Busy cwd:** a read-write resume into a locked cwd follows the #9 BUSY ruling (stderr `BUSY <holder>`, exit 3).\n--\n=== ISSUE 11 ===\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings (owner, 2026-10-01)\n\n1. **`delegate models`:** an aligned text table with id, label, backend and $in/$out per 1M tokens. The default is marked `*`. Rows sort by backend, then id.\n2. **`delegate doctor`:** human-readable text on stdout, one ok/warn/fail line per check. Missing or renamed models are warnings. It exits 0 when there are only warnings, and 1 on a hard failure (binary missing, or not logged in).\n3. **pi and claude models before #16/#17 land:** `run` exits 2 with `backend not implemented`, and `doctor` prints a skip line for each.\n4. **Model table:** `backend` replaces `family`. The ids are the 13 listed in #11 and spec story 45. Grok 4.7 is priced as Grok 4.6.\n--\n","localExecutionTimeMs":4518},"isBackground":false},"description":"View issues 7,9,10,11 with comments"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_e62da98b-fa48-4989-b8d9-9fb28291000","startedAtMs":"1790845451746","completedAtMs":"1790845457105"},"model_call_id":"e585ae89-c308-48e6-a816-313689ff8cab-0-gxxy","session_id":"7bb334b3-f226-467c-b3bf-a467f772d57f","timestamp_ms":1790845457077}
