{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**1. Contradictions**\n- #4/#7: no cross-session registry; `supervise` still uses `JobRegistry` and MCP `index.rs` remains. → **Delete MCP modules; supervisor owns job loop without registry.**\n- #13/`#4`: `DELEGATE_HOST_PROFILE`; code uses `CURSOR_DELEGATE_HOST_PROFILE`. → **Rename env; accept old name one release or drop.**\n- #13: drop old binary; `Cargo.toml` only builds `delegate` while `setup.sh`/`tests/e2e.rs` expect `cursor-delegate-mcp`. → **One `delegate` artifact; delete MCP e2e/parity.**\n- #7 #10: dual `delegate` bin; #13 removes old binary. → **Keep single `delegate` bin only.**\n- #13 plugin `1.0.0`; manifest `0.5.0` with `mcpServers`. → **1.0.0, skill-only, no MCP block.**\n\n**2. Unstated defaults**\n- PATH install target and method. → **`bin/delegate` symlink or copy into `~/.local/bin`.**\n- Profile migrate if destination exists. → **Skip if new file present; else move.**\n- Crate/package rename (`cursor-delegate-mcp`). → **Rename crate to `delegate` or document exception.**\n- Marketplace/plugin id strings. → **Rename to `delegate` / `delegate-local`.**\n\n**3. Failure cases**\n- Migrate with no old profile. → **No-op; scaffold minimal profile only if missing.**\n- Leftover `cursor-delegate-jobs` files. → **No migration; new runs use `delegate-jobs` only.**\n- `progress`/`validate`/`answer` callers after MCP delete. → **Remove with MCP; CLI uses `prompt` only.**\n\n**4. Acceptance criteria**\n- “No old-name references” vs migration/setup strings. → **Allow old paths only in migrate/setup comments.**\n- “Setup on this machine” vs CI. → **Treat as manual smoke; CI runs unit/cli tests only.**\n\nSTATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS"}]},"session_id":"7bb334b3-f226-467c-b3bf-a467f772d57f"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":64653,"duration_api_ms":64653,"is_error":false,"result":"Gathering GitHub issues, rulings, and relevant code from origin/main.\n\n\n**1. Contradictions**\n- #4/#7: no cross-session registry; `supervise` still uses `JobRegistry` and MCP `index.rs` remains. → **Delete MCP modules; supervisor owns job loop without registry.**\n- #13/`#4`: `DELEGATE_HOST_PROFILE`; code uses `CURSOR_DELEGATE_HOST_PROFILE`. → **Rename env; accept old name one release or drop.**\n- #13: drop old binary; `Cargo.toml` only builds `delegate` while `setup.sh`/`tests/e2e.rs` expect `cursor-delegate-mcp`. → **One `delegate` artifact; delete MCP e2e/parity.**\n- #7 #10: dual `delegate` bin; #13 removes old binary. → **Keep single `delegate` bin only.**\n- #13 plugin `1.0.0`; manifest `0.5.0` with `mcpServers`. → **1.0.0, skill-only, no MCP block.**\n\n**2. Unstated defaults**\n- PATH install target and method. → **`bin/delegate` symlink or copy into `~/.local/bin`.**\n- Profile migrate if destination exists. → **Skip if new file present; else move.**\n- Crate/package rename (`cursor-delegate-mcp`). → **Rename crate to `delegate` or document exception.**\n- Marketplace/plugin id strings. → **Rename to `delegate` / `delegate-local`.**\n\n**3. Failure cases**\n- Migrate with no old profile. → **No-op; scaffold minimal profile only if missing.**\n- Leftover `cursor-delegate-jobs` files. → **No migration; new runs use `delegate-jobs` only.**\n- `progress`/`validate`/`answer` callers after MCP delete. → **Remove with MCP; CLI uses `prompt` only.**\n\n**4. Acceptance criteria**\n- “No old-name references” vs migration/setup strings. → **Allow old paths only in migrate/setup comments.**\n- “Setup on this machine” vs CI. → **Treat as manual smoke; CI runs unit/cli tests only.**\n\nSTATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS","session_id":"7bb334b3-f226-467c-b3bf-a467f772d57f","request_id":"e585ae89-c308-48e6-a816-313689ff8cab","usage":{"inputTokens":42460,"outputTokens":4